        "text": "Here's a summary of the **Agent Builder SOP**:\n\n---\n\n## 🤖 Agent Builder — SOP Summary\n\n### 🧠 Core Philosophy\n> **\"The model already knows how to be an agent. Your job is to get out of the way.\"**\n\nAn agent is simply a loop:\n1. Model sees **context + capabilities**\n2. Model decides to **act or respond**\n3. If act → execute, add result, repeat; If respond → return to user\n\n---\n\n### 🔩 Three Core Elements\n| Element | What It Is | Design Principle |\n|--------|-----------|-----------------|\n| **Capabilities** | Atomic actions (search, read, create, send...) | Start with **3–5 only**; add more when failures demand it |\n| **Knowledge** | Domain expertise (policies, workflows, schemas) | Load **on-demand**, not upfront |\n| **Context** | Conversation history | Keep it **clean & clear**; isolate noisy subtasks |\n\n---\n\n### 📐 Design Thinking (Before Building)\nAsk yourself:\n- **Purpose** — What should the agent accomplish?\n- **Domain** — What world does it operate in?\n- **Capabilities** — What 3–5 actions are essential?\n- **Knowledge** — What expertise does it need?\n- **Trust** — What decisions can you delegate to the model?\n\n---\n\n### 📈 Progressive Complexity (Start Simple!)\n| Level | Add | Only When... |\n|-------|-----|-------------|\n| **Basic** | 3–5 capabilities | Always start here |\n| **Planning** | Progress tracking | Multi-step tasks lose coherence |\n| **Subagents** | Isolated child agents | Exploration pollutes context |\n| **Skills** | On-demand knowledge | Domain expertise is needed |\n\n> ⚠️ **Most agents never need to go beyond Level 2.**\n\n---\n\n### ✅ Key Principles\n1. **The model IS the agent** — code just runs the loop\n2. **Capabilities enable** — what it *can* do\n3. **Knowledge informs** — what it *knows* how to do\n4. **Constraints focus** — limits create clarity\n5. **Trust liberates** — let the model reason\n6. **Iteration reveals** — start minimal, evolve from real usage\n\n---\n\n### 🚫 Anti-Patterns to Avoid\n| Anti-Pattern | Problem | Fix |\n|---|---|---|\n| Over-engineering | Complexity before need | Start simple |\n| Too many capabilities | Model confusion | Stick to 3–5 |\n| Rigid workflows | Can't adapt | Let model decide |\n| Front-loaded knowledge | Context bloat | Load on-demand |\n| Micromanagement | Undercuts intelligence | Trust the model |\n\n---\n\n### 💡 The Agent Mindset Shift\n- ❌ *\"How do I make the system do X?\"*\n- ✅ *\"How do I **enable the model** to do X?\"*\n\nThe best agent code is almost **boring** — simple loops, clear capabilities, clean context. **The magic is in the model, not the code.**",
